    "narrative": "A 70-year-old man suffered a ground-level fall at home resulting in a left hip fracture. He underwent a left femoral neck fixation with hemiarthroplasty. Postoperatively, he experienced medical complications including respiratory insufficiency, perioperative anemia, pneumonia, and hypertension, which were managed closely with cardiology and medical consultations. He responded well to medical treatment alongside physical and occupational therapy, gradually tolerating increased activity. Currently, he is doing well with clear lungs, a regular cardiac rhythm, a healed wound with staples removed, and normal lower extremity neurological exam. The plan is to transfer him to rehab as soon as medically cleared.",
